course: dictionary
lesson: 14110
title: Messaging: two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one you need. «I spent an hour messaging my friends about the football match.» Here messaging means sending texts or messages on a phone or computer.
explain: Messaging can also mean the way a politician or a company chooses its words to make people think a certain way. «The minister's messaging made a small mistake sound like a big success.» The clues are small mistake and big success: the words were picked to change how people see the mistake. This is called spin.
explain: Grown-ups who work in politics and advertising use this kind of messaging, so it is jargon, a special word used in one type of work. Ask yourself: is the sentence about phones, or about how something is presented? Then try your meaning in the sentence and see if it makes sense.
fact: Messaging has two main meanings.
fact: «Messaging» (everyday meaning) means sending texts or online messages.
fact: «Messaging» (jargon meaning) means the way words are chosen to make people think a certain way. This is also called spin.
fact: If the sentence is about phones or screens, messaging means texting. If it is about how words are chosen to influence people, it means spin.
exercise: «I spent an hour messaging my friends about the football match.» What does messaging mean here? | Drawing pictures | Walking slowly | *Sending texts or online messages | Choosing words to make people think a certain way
exercise: «The company's messaging made a late delivery sound like a special gift.» What does messaging mean here? | Riding a bike to work | Packing parcels into boxes | *The way words are chosen to make people think a certain way | Sending texts on a phone
exercise: Mia says, «Messaging just means texting, right?» What is the best answer? | *No, it can also mean how words are chosen to shape what people think | No, it means singing loudly | Only if you are using a computer | Yes, it always means texting
test: «The minister's messaging made a small mistake sound like a big success.» What does messaging mean in this sentence? | Writing letters by hand | *The way words are chosen to make people think a certain way | Driving a car carefully | Sending texts to friends
test: «Ben kept messaging his gran every evening.» What does messaging mean in this sentence? | *Sending texts or online messages | Choosing words to shape what people think | Gardening in the garden | Singing in the school choir
exam: «The advert's messaging made cheap juice sound like the healthiest drink in the world.» What does messaging mean here? | Mixing drinks at a party | Sending texts about juice | Shopping in a supermarket | *The way words are chosen to make people think a certain way
